-- title:
--   Quadratic relations for the six words in a dicyclic pair
-- statement:
--   Let $V$ be an additive abelian group and let $\alpha,\beta\colon V\to V$ be additive endomorphisms subject to the pointwise relations $\alpha(\alpha T)=-T$, $\beta(\beta T)+\beta T+T=0$ and $\alpha(\beta T)=\beta(\beta(\alpha T))$ for all $T\in V$; thus $\alpha^2=-1$, $\beta^2+\beta+1=0$ and $\alpha\beta=\beta^2\alpha$ as endomorphisms. Let $m\colon V\to V$ be an additive endomorphism which is one of the six words $\mathrm{id}$, $\alpha$, $\beta$, $T\mapsto\beta(\beta T)$, $T\mapsto\alpha(\beta T)$, $T\mapsto\alpha(\beta(\beta T))$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an integer $t$ with $t\in\{-1,0,1,2\}$, such that $t=2$ forces $m=\mathrm{id}$, and such that $m$ satisfies the quadratic relation $m(m\,T)-t\cdot m\,T+T=0$ for every $T\in V$, the scalar action being that of $\mathbb{Z}$ on $V$. In other words each of the six words satisfies $m^2-tm+1=0$ on $V$ for a trace $t$ in the listed set, with the value $t=2$ occurring only for the identity.
--
--   A purely algebraic lemma about the group generated by two endomorphisms satisfying the relations of the dicyclic group of order $12$, realised in the intended application by the automorphisms of the supersingular curve $y^2=x^3-x$ in characteristic $3$ acting on points. It is used by [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_int_transport_comp_sub_smul_add_eq_zero_of_j_eq_zero_of_charP_three`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_int_transport_comp_sub_smul_add_eq_zero_of_j_eq_zero_of_charP_three), which supplies a quadratic relation with integral trace for transport maps attached to curves of $j$-invariant $0$ in characteristic $3$.
-- source:
